Bundled third-party notices
---------------------------

License texts for everything bundled into a build are generated at build time into
`third-party-licenses.json`, which the app renders under Settings > Open source
licenses. `third-party-licenses/spdx/` holds the SPDX texts the generator renders with.

Two bundled entries are worth naming explicitly when redistributing a build:

- heic-to 1.5.2, LGPL-3.0-or-later, https://github.com/hoppergee/heic-to
  Unmodified. Decodes HEIC images in the web client, so it is part of the web and
  desktop bundles. Its license text is included in the generated manifest. To replace
  it, swap the dependency in `apps/web/package.json` and rebuild; no other component
  has to change.
- KaTeX mathematical fonts and Carlito (OFL-1.1), bundled unmodified. The reserved
  font names are listed in the generated notices.

Everything else in a build is MIT, Apache-2.0, BSD-2-Clause, BSD-3-Clause, ISC, CC0-1.0,
or Unlicense.